{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/840462-could-an-incarna-make-use-of-an-exigent-exaltation","id":840462,"title":"Could an Incarna make use of an Exigent Exaltation?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Exigents"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-02T00:29:38-08:00","id":840462,"title":"Could an Incarna make use of an Exigent Exaltation?","content":"So I'm wondering could say Mars make use of an Exigent Exaltation to make a one off Exalted of War or Battle? <br /> <br /> Could two or more Gods make use of a Single Exaltation of Exigency? I'm guessing no. But I'm wondering say say spirits synchronized like say the God of a Field combined with a God of Harvest and the God of Wheat? Or the God of Shadows with the God of Silence?<br /> <br /> And I recall it being answered only Gods can use Exigency so I can't make one offs spawned by one of the Elementals Dragons, or Gaia?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T00:48:51-08:00","id":840476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/840462-could-an-incarna-make-use-of-an-exigent-exaltation#post840462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I'm wondering could say Mars make use of an Exigent Exaltation to make a one off Exalted of War or Battle?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. The Exigence is how lesser gods are able to choose their Exalted. The Incarnae wielded that power more directly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Could two or more Gods make use of a Single Exaltation of Exigency? I'm guessing no. But I'm wondering say say spirits synchronized like say the God of a Field combined with a God of Harvest and the God of Wheat? Or the God of Shadows with the God of Silence? </div> </div> </div>Yes, but that's definitely in black market exigent territory. Like, really really deep in it. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T01:04:59-08:00","id":840480,"title":"","content":"Mars has Exalts of War and Battle. They're called Sidereals, specifically the Chosen of Mars, or the Shieldbearers.<br /> <br /> Now, if you wanted to say, make a Chosen of a War God, nothing stopping you from saying that Ahlat or Tien-Yu got hold of an Exigence.<br /> <br /> (Man, can you imagine playing an Exigent of Tien-Yu in Lookshy? That'd be AWESOME)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T01:59:19-08:00","id":840490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/840462-could-an-incarna-make-use-of-an-exigent-exaltation#post840462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I'm wondering could say Mars make use of an Exigent Exaltation to make a one off Exalted of War or Battle?<br /> <br /> Could two or more Gods make use of a Single Exaltation of Exigency? I'm guessing no. But I'm wondering say say spirits synchronized like say the God of a Field combined with a God of Harvest and the God of Wheat? Or the God of Shadows with the God of Silence?<br /> <br /> And I recall it being answered only Gods can use Exigency so I can't make one offs spawned by one of the Elementals Dragons, or Gaia?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think do whatever you think gives you a cool story.<br /> <br /> At the end of the day nothing is going to break in the game if their is a war themed exalt from Mars that isn't a Sideral. Make sure they feel unique and don't to it too often and put the thaught into the back story, but after that go for it.<br /> <br /> A story about a lone mars exalt trying to figure out why they are and some of the sids hating it for being different and some embracing it for being a cousin/sibling could potentially be cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2325-builder","name":"Builder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2325_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T05:07:45-08:00","id":840565,"title":"","content":"The devs have shot it down before, but you feel free to do it in your game; it's not like they can stop you\u2026 yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T05:25:23-08:00","id":840574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Builder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/840462-could-an-incarna-make-use-of-an-exigent-exaltation?p=840490#post840490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think do whatever you think gives you a cool story.<br /> <br /> At the end of the day nothing is going to break in the game if their is a war themed exalt from Mars that isn't a Sideral. Make sure they feel unique and don't to it too often and put the thaught into the back story, but after that go for it.<br /> <br /> A story about a lone mars exalt trying to figure out why they are and some of the sids hating it for being different and some embracing it for being a cousin/sibling could potentially be cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>what a particular table does is no issue. It just shouldn't be canon. As we have no idea of people's house rules unless they tell us, this forum tends to give the canon answer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T05:32:28-08:00","id":840577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/840462-could-an-incarna-make-use-of-an-exigent-exaltation?p=840565#post840565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it's not like they can stop you\u2026 yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Canon ninjas are supposed to be a stretch goal for the Sidereal hardback Kickstarter, so we've got some time until they arrive.<br /> <br /> That said, the idea reeks of super speshul snowflake - &quot;oh, I'm not one of the twenty Chosen of Battles, I'm the one and only, unique Chosen of Mars herself!&quot; Me no likey.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T06:11:30-08:00","id":840592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/840462-could-an-incarna-make-use-of-an-exigent-exaltation?p=840577#post840577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, the idea reeks of super speshul snowflake - &quot;oh, I'm not one of the twenty Chosen of Battles, I'm the one and only, unique Chosen of Mars herself!&quot; Me no likey.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually feel sorry for an Exigent of Mars. You know the Maidens would have some strange plan that is bound not to end well for the poor Exigent.<br /> <br /> Though I imagine the conversation between the Unconquered Sun and Mars would be interesting.<br /> <br /> UCS: So....You want an Exigent. Don't you have twenty other chosen already? What happened to them?<br /> Mars: Nothing... It's just... They are all assholes.<br /> UCS: Didn't you choose them yourself?<br /> Mars: Yes! Even I didn't foresee them turning into a bunch of dicks!<br /> Venus: I did!<br /> Mars: Shut up, Venus!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 03-02-2016, 09:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T06:16:46-08:00","id":840594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/840462-could-an-incarna-make-use-of-an-exigent-exaltation?p=840592#post840592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually feel sorry for an Exigent of Mars. You know the Maidens would have some strange plan that is bound not to end well for the poor Exigent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, I'm gonna tick off &quot;mysterious and dark destiny awaiting&quot; on the Speshul Snowflake Checklist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T06:21:52-08:00","id":840596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/840462-could-an-incarna-make-use-of-an-exigent-exaltation?p=840594#post840594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right, I'm gonna tick off &quot;mysterious and dark destiny awaiting&quot; on the Speshul Snowflake Checklist.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, yeah. I'm sure the power gamer who wants to play this concept just wants to play a Chosen of Battles without the baggage of playing a Sidereal. Arcane Fate can be a drag sometimes.<br /> <br /> This is my big fear for Exigents honestly. Powergamers just wanting custom OP charmsets and ability combos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 03-02-2016, 09:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T06:28:50-08:00","id":840600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/840462-could-an-incarna-make-use-of-an-exigent-exaltation?p=840596#post840596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, yeah. I'm sure the power gamer who wants to play this concept just wants to play a Chosen of Battles without the baggage of playing a Sidereal. Arcane Fate can be a drag sometimes.<br /> <br /> This is my big fear for Exigents honestly. Powergamers just wanting custom OP charmsets and ability combos.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, the nebulous but dreadful specter of &quot;power gamers.&quot; <br /> <br /> Look, a shitty Exigent Charmset is going to be shitty but at least it only affects one table, much like a vast majority of the Devil Tiger Charmsets out there. And yet all Solars are inherently ideal for powergaming straight out of the core, with nowhere near the number of complaints about that, so let's just let this mound-of-paste-that-used-to-be-a-horse-corpse lie and not fall into things like the Stormwind Fallacy or the notion that wanting a powerful character is somehow BadWrongFun. <br /> <br /> Or if you're the ST and a player does bring a shitty OP Exigent set, simply reject it, which is well within your rights.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T06:30:05-08:00","id":840602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Builder</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">nothing is going to break</div> </div> </div> </div> Just your pour oul mother's heart. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T06:40:16-08:00","id":840607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/840462-could-an-incarna-make-use-of-an-exigent-exaltation#post840462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I recall it being answered only Gods can use Exigency so I can't make one offs spawned by one of the Elementals Dragons</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they already have Exalts. What else is Hesiah going to make? The Chosen of More Fire?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":2093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","user":"Crumplepunch","date":". 03-02-2016, 09:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T06:46:26-08:00","id":840610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/840462-could-an-incarna-make-use-of-an-exigent-exaltation?p=840600#post840600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or if you're the ST and a player does bring a shitty OP Exigent set, simply reject it, which is well within your rights.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I run a game, Exigents are not going to be allowed at the table. Mostly because I lack the mechanical knowhow to distinguish between a balanced charm set and a shitty OP charmset.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T06:53:45-08:00","id":840615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/840462-could-an-incarna-make-use-of-an-exigent-exaltation#post840462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I recall it being answered only Gods can use Exigency so I can't make one offs spawned by one of the Elementals Dragons, or Gaia?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Exigence is limited to the gods, However, there's nothing stopping you coming up with, for example, a demonic equivalent to the Exigence, and using the Exigents book to build these Exalted.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T07:26:21-08:00","id":840637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/840462-could-an-incarna-make-use-of-an-exigent-exaltation?p=840596#post840596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well, yeah. I'm sure the power gamer who wants to play this concept just wants to play a Chosen of Battles without the baggage of playing a Sidereal. Arcane Fate can be a drag sometimes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can empathize with people who might want to do this for thematic reasons rather than just power gaming ones.<br /> <br /> Sidereal are Chosen of all the Maidens. When a Chosen of Endings approaches Performance rolls, they do so through the prism of Venus. When they engage in war, they do that through Mars' prism.<br /> <br /> I can understand why someone might want to play a character who approaches everything through the themes of Saturn or Mars and would want to make a Chosen of one Maiden rather than all of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T07:38:36-08:00","id":840647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/840462-could-an-incarna-make-use-of-an-exigent-exaltation?p=840610#post840610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I run a game, Exigents are not going to be allowed at the table. Mostly because I lack the mechanical knowhow to distinguish between a balanced charm set and a shitty OP charmset.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's absolutely fair!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T08:29:18-08:00","id":840671,"title":"","content":"The whole point is ... it doesn't have to be Exigent, it could be some &quot;other&quot; type of Exaltation. You are in homebrew territory anyway, it was explicitly stated that the reason behind the new Exalted was to show us that there are strange things out there that do not fit the classic roles. Are there Exalted that derive their power from Isthvara or some other deeper myths?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/744-korusef","name":"Korusef","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar744_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"510"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T08:50:43-08:00","id":840688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korusef</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/840462-could-an-incarna-make-use-of-an-exigent-exaltation?p=840671#post840671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The whole point is ... it doesn't have to be Exigent, it could be some &quot;other&quot; type of Exaltation. You are in homebrew territory anyway, it was explicitly stated that the reason behind the new Exalted was to show us that there are strange things out there that do not fit the classic roles. Are there Exalted that derive their power from Isthvara or some other deeper myths?</div> </div> </div> </div>Can't speak for the others, but my objection to the &quot;Exigent of an Incarna/Elemental Dragons&quot; idea has little to do with whether they're called Exigent or not, and everything to do with the setting implications of letting the patrons of established Exalted types getting to do a second take on creating their Chosen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T09:56:59-08:00","id":840735,"title":"","content":"As a matter of canon, it's clearly a bad idea to have the Incarnae use Exigence to get a &quot;do over.&quot; That takes the narrative spotlight away from the intended protagonists, really.<br /> <br /> For individual stories, though, it's got some great narrative legs. I wouldn't allow an Exigent of Mars in a game with any Sid PCs, but with a good backstory I would let it fly. Similarly, if I was running a game set before the breaking of the Jade Prison, an Exigent of Sol could be interesting.<br /> <br /> One of my shelved ideas for my current game of mortals was to Exalt them with Exigence from TUS to go find the Prison and break it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T18:59:48-08:00","id":841059,"title":"","content":"Regarding canon, I think the Maidens (and their purviews) are too inextricably linked for one among them to really make an Exigent on her own. Journeys, conflicts, secrets, serenity, and resolution all sort of flow into and through one another in a way that's really hard to isolate a single part of. Especially when also filtering these through the lens of the Loom of Fate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T19:37:05-08:00","id":841066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/840462-could-an-incarna-make-use-of-an-exigent-exaltation?p=840637#post840637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can empathize with people who might want to do this for thematic reasons rather than just power gaming ones.<br /> <br /> Sidereal are Chosen of all the Maidens. When a Chosen of Endings approaches Performance rolls, they do so through the prism of Venus. When they engage in war, they do that through Mars' prism.<br /> <br /> I can understand why someone might want to play a character who approaches everything through the themes of Saturn or Mars and would want to make a Chosen of one Maiden rather than all of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>For that purpose, there's always the option of choosing or creating a god who's closely thematically linked with an Incarna, such as Yaogin or the Golden Lord.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T12:59:31-08:00","id":841455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/840462-could-an-incarna-make-use-of-an-exigent-exaltation#post840462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I'm wondering could say Mars make use of an Exigent Exaltation to make a one off Exalted of War or Battle?</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I wouldn't allow the Incarna to create more Exalted/Exigents from themselves. However, it may be possible for Mars to get her hands on a black market exigence/exaltation and fix up an Exigent of her using that stolen power. Why she would do such a thing though is the big question. I would also make this exigent weaker in power than sidereals. Maybe terrestrial exalted power level.<br /> <br /> I could, and this is a stretch, see the Maiden of Endings or Secrets making use of such an agent. Someone she could use to carry out some of her work on the dl that she doesn't want to risk her sidereals for. It may be handy for Endings to have a supernatural assassin who isn't a sidereal.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Good night sweet Green Sun Prince: And flights of demons beat thee to thy rest...with billyclubs! <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/362-darkon","name":"Darkon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar362_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T14:30:52-08:00","id":841506,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure part of the point of the limitations is to give non-incarna gods some spotlight and encourage players to be creative.<br /> <br /> &quot;Chosen of Mars but not sidereal&quot; just stagnates the game more, as it wastes what's meant to be an awesome opportunity to create a God with interesting themes, relationships and back-story in favor of more of the same. The world is vast and alive, not everything revolves around the incarnae/yozi.<br /> <br /> Friends don't let friends make knockoff exigents.<br /> <br /> Edit: although... An exigent of knock-offs....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T14:37:28-08:00","id":841509,"title":"","content":"I'll admit I have an idea for a Exigent of Artificial Flight which may end up being a knock off Twilight Crafter. If you can't build your own charms, then rip them off from something else!<br /> <br /> /That excuse isn't going to fly with Storyteller.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T14:50:52-08:00","id":841515,"title":"","content":"No said they were the same as previous kosher Exaltations. Assuming so is on you brohams.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T15:44:41-08:00","id":841541,"title":"","content":"How is an Exigent of Mars different from a Chosen of Battles, then? How is an Exigent of the Unconquered Sun different from a Solar?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T16:10:07-08:00","id":841552,"title":"","content":"The official answer has already been given, &quot;no Incarnae can create an Exigent&quot;. If you want to change it for your table, you're more then welcome too. Debating whether it should be possible in canon is pointless, as it's not going to happen.<br /> <br /> The possibility of an Exigent from more then one minor god was already confirmed as possible too. As for how it works, you'll have to wait for the Exigent book because the best we can do is speculate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T16:19:36-08:00","id":841558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/840462-could-an-incarna-make-use-of-an-exigent-exaltation?p=841541#post841541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How is an Exigent of Mars different from a Chosen of Battles, then? How is an Exigent of the Unconquered Sun different from a Solar?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> By designing a brand new Exalt off the Theme of Battle or War. Pretty much the same as how you make any Exigent. The only way it would be the same is if you just copy and paste all the Sidereal Mechanics... Hell you could even use the thematics of 2nd ed Green Sun Princes but modeled as Mars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T16:20:44-08:00","id":841560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/840462-could-an-incarna-make-use-of-an-exigent-exaltation?p=841552#post841552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The official answer has already been given, &quot;no Incarnae can create an Exigent&quot;. If you want to change it for your table, you're more then welcome too. Debating whether it should be possible in canon is pointless, as it's not going to happen.<br /> <br /> The possibility of an Exigent from more then one minor god was already confirmed as possible too. As for how it works, you'll have to wait for the Exigent book because the best we can do is speculate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm confused do you not want this thread to continue? I am getting a sense you want me to drop all discussion for some reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T16:28:17-08:00","id":841564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/840462-could-an-incarna-make-use-of-an-exigent-exaltation?p=841558#post841558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By designing a brand new Exalt off the Theme of Battle or War. Pretty much the same as how you make any Exigent.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not how you make an Exigent (well, might be how <i>you</i> do it, but the devs have described a very different process). An Exigent is not the Chosen of Lookshy, he's the Chosen of Tien-Yu. Not the Chosen of Dice, but the Chosen of Plentimon. Not the Chosen of Elsewhere, but the Chosen of Madame Marthesine of the Lost. <br /> <br /> The purview is but one flavor in the making of an Exigent - the nature and attitudes of the god are so much more than that. Thing is, picking &quot;battles&quot; or &quot;warfare&quot; <i>is not going to net you an interesting Exigent</i>, because <i>warfare is not a person</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T16:46:31-08:00","id":841576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/840462-could-an-incarna-make-use-of-an-exigent-exaltation?p=841564#post841564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not how you make an Exigent (well, might be how <i>you</i> do it, but the devs have described a very different process). An Exigent is not the Chosen of Lookshy, he's the Chosen of Tien-Yu. Not the Chosen of Dice, but the Chosen of Plentimon. Not the Chosen of Elsewhere, but the Chosen of Madame Marthesine of the Lost.<br /> <br /> The purview is but one flavor in the making of an Exigent - the nature and attitudes of the god are so much more than that. Thing is, picking &quot;battles&quot; or &quot;warfare&quot; <i>is not going to net you an interesting Exigent</i>, because <i>warfare is not a person</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>It really seems to me like you are intentionally choosing to interpret posts of few words looking for conflict. And you are make really specific inferences.<br /> <br /> Clearly I am talking about a Chosen of Mars, as it is an Exigent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T16:47:50-08:00","id":841577,"title":"","content":"And? What's this hypothetical Chosen of Only Mars look like?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T16:51:46-08:00","id":841579,"title":"","content":"? You do know I'm not making an actual character right? I mean it is literally just an example. Exalted can look like essentially anything, Exigents especially. I mean you do realize this is a fictional game right. And two people can come up with ideas for Exigents of the same god and do it differently in two different games. Its made to be pretty interpretive, and a tool for use of personal games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T17:11:58-08:00","id":841591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/840462-could-an-incarna-make-use-of-an-exigent-exaltation?p=840610#post840610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If I run a game, Exigents are not going to be allowed at the table. Mostly because I lack the mechanical knowhow to distinguish between a balanced charm set and a shitty OP charmset.</div> </div> </div> </div>They won't ever be allowed at my table either. Frankly I do have the knowhow, but if I'm trying to put together a game I have neither the time nor inclination.<br /> <br /> This is coming from a massive infernal fan who didn't like Devil Tigers for much the same reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1414-pyrosorc","name":"Pyrosorc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T17:29:14-08:00","id":841598,"title":"","content":"If I was writing up an Exigent of Battles, I'd make them like a Sidereal who could only use Battles Colleges and Battles Abilities. Plus Martial Arts and Sorcery, of course.<br /> <br /> Part of the reason for this approach is that thematically, I think it's a good thing if the Chosen of Mars Alone are clearly inferior to the Sidereal Exalted. Another part is that using only a part of the Sidereal Charmset emphasizes the &quot;hammering nails in with a screwdriver&quot; angle that the Charmset already promotes. But the biggest part is that it would save me a lot of work.<br /> <br /> EDIT: And while we're on the topic, I'm really interested in Exigents largely because it sounds like such a bad idea. Most people can't homebrew worth a damn: if Exigents can teach the average player to make a playable splat I will be extremely impressed. It's an incredibly ambitious book, and I for one have high hopes for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":1154,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","user":"Sanctaphrax","date":". 03-03-2016, 08:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T17:50:05-08:00","id":841612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/840462-could-an-incarna-make-use-of-an-exigent-exaltation?p=841598#post841598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> EDIT: And while we're on the topic, I'm really interested in Exigents largely because it sounds like such a bad idea. Most people can't homebrew worth a damn: if Exigents can teach the average player to make a playable splat I will be extremely impressed. It's an incredibly ambitious book, and I for one have high hopes for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sanctaphrax, you are a scholar and a gentleman.<br /> <br /> I will say this; in my experience, players are really, really good at expanding an already-drawn map. I've had very few players who, after they acquired a decent amount of experience with a given Exalt types Charmtree, couldn't make up a whole bunch of relatively well-balanced Charms that branched off it.<br /> <br /> Indeed, I can't speak for other GMs... but a few of my favorite moments have been when a player went &quot;Mmmmrrrrr... these Charms aren't quite doing what I want them to do.&quot; and I reminded them that they could <i>make their own</i>, and suddenly they remembered that was a <i>thing</i> and were like &quot;FUCK YEAH YOU HAND ME A GODDAMN PENCIL.&quot;<br /> <br /> I have very tentatively been of the opinion for some time that the Exigents are going to live or die based on the strength of whatever templates they provide. If those are of sufficient robustness and utility, people will be able to take them and fold, spindle, and mutilate into whatever they need, which is usually way easier than starting with a white sheet of paper and a concept. If they are not, people are really going to struggle.<br /> <br /> And y'know, even in the latter case, that might be okay. The Exigent book might be very, very demanding to use. That's fine! These are obscure, one-off Exalts of individual gods, which means they're easily ignorable at-table. It's okay to have a splat that isn't for everyone as long as it doesn't suck.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T18:31:51-08:00","id":841635,"title":"","content":"I noticed in the Core, the exigent of the God of Wu-Jian was referred to several times as an Architect.<br /> <br /> This suggests to me that maybe the Exigent book will include several templates for people to base stuff on, and Architect is the city-god exigent. After all, many of her charms are charms that could apply to most cities. Maybe stuff like the red-light district charm doesn't apply to every one, but it'll still apply to most, as would the charm for getting soak from the stone of the city. So it'd seem easier for the book to include a bunch of city-based charms that most city-exigents could take, which can then be modified or added to for the specific god or goddess in question.<br /> <br /> Similarly, perhaps charms for war gods, charms for terrestrial nature gods maybe, and so on.<br /> <br /> I think you are quite right Mercushio, having nothing to base it on would be too difficult, and I would not at all be confident when a player brought me their charms for approval.<br /> Not to mention... it's a ton of work for both player and ST.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T18:36:02-08:00","id":841638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/840462-could-an-incarna-make-use-of-an-exigent-exaltation?p=841509#post841509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll admit I have an idea for a Exigent of Artificial Flight which may end up being a knock off Twilight Crafter. If you can't build your own charms, then rip them off from something else!<br /> <br /> /That excuse isn't going to fly with Storyteller.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vanileth was going to be my first or second Exigent (Agralzo being the other contender). I imagine the athletic and combat trees would show it a little more though. Like an attack charm that lets you jump into the air and hover to shoot over cover or a movement charm that makes you float a few inches of the ground and glide.<br /> <br /> The crafting will probably have the sort of wonky problems Infernals did, and suck at making personal scale equipment but great for making things that combine well with flying machines. Perhaps any Diaklave you forge also has to double as an essence glider wing. (Because who doesn't love blade wings?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T18:50:37-08:00","id":841644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/840462-could-an-incarna-make-use-of-an-exigent-exaltation?p=841638#post841638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Vanileth was going to be my first or second Exigent (Agralzo being the other contender). I imagine the athletic and combat trees would show it a little more though. Like an attack charm that lets you jump into the air and hover to shoot over cover or a movement charm that makes you float a few inches of the ground and glide.<br /> <br /> The crafting will probably have the sort of wonky problems Infernals did, and suck at making personal scale equipment but great for making things that combine well with flying machines. Perhaps any Diaklave you forge also has to double as an essence glider wing. (Because who doesn't love blade wings?)</div> </div> </div> </div>My concept was more of an intellectual social character whose goal was to expand artificial flight in Creation. Sort of in the vein of The Right Stuff, October Skies, and As the Wind Rises. Atheltics would definitely be a favored skill along with thrown. Her Anima would be paper cranes fluttering about her. <br /> <br /> Originally I had her be a Lookshian; when I looked up the God of artifical flight, he is based in the heslanti league. In hindsight she would make a good NPC in a Solar game, since the character is so focused. The circle could trade favors with her.<br /> <br /> My big barrier is designing the charm set. Might just steal craft, Atheltics, and thrown charms from the solar charm set. The god of artificial flight is powerful enough and lost enough status to empower a Celestial level champion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 03-03-2016, 09:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T04:19:33-08:00","id":841811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/840462-could-an-incarna-make-use-of-an-exigent-exaltation?p=841579#post841579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">? You do know I'm not making an actual character right? I mean it is literally just an example. Exalted can look like essentially anything, Exigents especially. I mean you do realize this is a fictional game right. And two people can come up with ideas for Exigents of the same god and do it differently in two different games. Its made to be pretty interpretive, and a tool for use of personal games.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Be that as it may, I am honestly curious as to how you imagine this Chosen of Mars differing from the twenty that already exist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T04:42:49-08:00","id":841823,"title":"","content":"To me the major complication with a Devil Tiger was that you kept all your old Yozi charms and had to work in your new theme around them.<br /> <br /> For example: A Scourge Caste speed demon becomes a Devil Tiger so that\u2019s obviously going to be a major theme for them. But by this point they\u2019ve already got all the Adorjan charms for directly increasing their speed. So should you be stacking even more speed boosters with your existing ones? Or should you be expressing the theme differently?<br /> <br /> As such, Exigents look easier to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 03-04-2016, 07:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T05:53:12-08:00","id":842502,"title":"","content":"Obviously the official answer to &quot;Incarnae making Exigents&quot; is always going to be &quot;no, that's badwrongfun&quot;, because the idea of having the REAL chosen of [Maiden X] / Luna / the Unconquered Sun running around is not really fun for people who play the existing splats that have those as their patron. I mean, nobody can stop you from doing it in your game, but as something in the default setting the problems are obvious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T07:06:36-08:00","id":842539,"title":"","content":"I think that problem could be avoided by making the Exigents clearly inferior to the existing splats.<br /> <br /> I suggested earlier that an Exigent of Battles would be one-fifth of a Sidereal. I don't think that method would work for Lunars or Solars though.<br /> <br /> Maybe Exigents of Luna and Sol could acquire weaknesses from their patrons that Lunars and Solars don't. So a Solar Exigent would be like a real Solar, except bound by rules and Virtues and such in a way that noticeably weakens them. And a Lunar Exigent would be like a Lunar half gone to Chimerism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T08:43:33-08:00","id":842588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/840462-could-an-incarna-make-use-of-an-exigent-exaltation?p=842539#post842539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that problem could be avoided by making the Exigents clearly inferior to the existing splats.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, that doesn't fix it.<br /> <br /> At the end of the day, if you've got an Incarnae suddenly deciding to create a new type of Exalted, it's going to be hard to avoid the implication that this is their &quot;true&quot; Exalted, and hard to avoid the implication of cheapening what it means to be chosen by an Incarnae. I mean -- why are they doing this now? What's the point?<br /> <br /> If your answer is &quot;they just want more power&quot;, <i>ugh</i>. Fine, I'll explain: Part of the purpose of 3e's changes to Exaltation are, I think, to avoid cheapening the Exalted. Exalted are chosen heroes, and Exaltation is a transcendent miracle; it's not a cruise missile. The idea of Luna saying &quot;well, the Lunars are <i>pretty good</i>, but, you know, every little bit helps, so I'm going to squeeze a bit more Exaltation out of the end of the tube and throw some cut-rate New Exalted of Luna out there to help them&quot; inherently cheapens the concept of Exalted and the idea that Luna made an actual meaningful statement by naming the Lunars as her chosen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T09:01:15-08:00","id":842593,"title":"","content":"I kind of wonder about that logic of the *real* Chosen, since who's to say the originals aren't realer just because an Incarna made another form of Chosen recently? If anything, it's harder to avoid the implication that a recent Exalt would be a mere inauthentic Johnny Come Lately.<br /> <br /> I suspect that if it is a problem, it's more because it undermines the idea that each of the Chosen *fully* represent the Incarna. That is, it's not that an Exigent of Incarna would be realer, but that everyone becomes less &quot;real&quot;, because they're all only embodying partial parts of their gods, a &quot;take&quot; on their Chosen, rather than definitive and platonic.<br /> <br /> (I'm not sure I agree with this though - like for instance, if you want to introduce a Solar who works through Attributes, I think the real hurdle is more why the Unconquered Sun would wish to do this and take the lessening when his Chosen who use skill should be adequate to the task, not that any of them would feel less or more real).<br /> <br /> IIRC, for the Unconquered Sun in particular though, I think it's also true that Exigents do already offer a way to have different Chosen of the Sun, so long as they're flavored by another god, since every Exigent is, in a sense, the Chosen of the Sun, and can be potentially quite strongly marked by his nature, if I understand the process correctly. So that sort of mellifies that he doesn't actually make Exigents that are his, for those that are looking for it. One mod that you could introduce to a game is also to have other Incarna involved in the Exigency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T09:03:22-08:00","id":842596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/840462-could-an-incarna-make-use-of-an-exigent-exaltation?p=842588#post842588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, that doesn't fix it.<br /> <br /> At the end of the day, if you've got an Incarnae suddenly deciding to create a new type of Exalted, it's going to be hard to avoid the implication that this is their &quot;true&quot; Exalted, and hard to avoid the implication of cheapening what it means to be chosen by an Incarnae. I mean -- why are they doing this now? What's the point?<br /> <br /> If your answer is &quot;they just want more power&quot;, <i>ugh</i>. Fine, I'll explain: Part of the purpose of 3e's changes to Exaltation are, I think, to avoid cheapening the Exalted. Exalted are chosen heroes, and Exaltation is a transcendent miracle; it's not a cruise missile. The idea of Luna saying &quot;well, the Lunars are <i>pretty good</i>, but, you know, every little bit helps, so I'm going to squeeze a bit more Exaltation out of the end of the tube and throw some cut-rate New Exalted of Luna out there to help them&quot; inherently cheapens the concept of Exalted and the idea that Luna made an actual meaningful statement by naming the Lunars as her chosen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct me if I am wrong, but there isn't a set number of Celestial Exalts* in Ex3. Maybe Luna and the UCS don't use Exigents because if they find someone they like, they just Exalt them as a Solar or Lunar. The reason why there are only 300- 400 Solars/Lunars in Creation is because that's all the people Lunar and the UC found worthy of their Exaltation.<br /> <br /> *I can see Sidereals being limited to a flat 20 per maiden. Silly Maidens liking everything neat and orderly. Of course the Maidens craft their Exalts though events in their lives. I don't see them giving the second breath to some Random Dude they haven't watched and mentored since this dude's first breath. Too risky.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 03-05-2016, 12:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T09:11:21-08:00","id":842598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/840462-could-an-incarna-make-use-of-an-exigent-exaltation?p=842593#post842593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's also true that Exigents do already offer a way to have different Chosen of the Sun, so long as they're flavored by another god, since every Exigent is, in a sense, the Chosen of the Sun, and can be potentially quite strongly marked by his nature, if I understand the process correctly. So that sort of mellifies that he doesn't actually make Exigents that are his, for those that are looking for it. One mod that you could introduce to a game is also to have other Incarna involved in the Exigency.</div> </div> </div> </div>This.<br /> <br /> The narrative purpose of the limitations on Exigency is there for you to go &quot;Okay, I want a Chosen of the Sun, but they can't be UCS's chosen. What other Sun-God can I use?&quot; And then you come up with the Chosen of Ra, Horus, Huitzilopochtli or Zhulong; all of which are very distinct from eachother (One of them is a friggin Sun-Dragon!) and lead to very different themes and make the game itself more interesting and developed at that table. It lets the player stamp the setting with their own god, indelibly changing it and inversting in it. Over time it builds pantheons and mythologies around long-term campaigns.<br /> <br /> All of which is scrapped by going &quot;Unconquered sun chose a non-solar because fuck those guys&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/840462-could-an-incarna-make-use-of-an-exigent-exaltation?p=842596#post842596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Correct me if I am wrong, but there isn't a set number of Celestial Exalts* in Ex3. Maybe Luna and the UCS don't use Exigents because if they find someone they like, they just Exalt them as a Solar or Lunar. The reason why there are only 300- 400 Solars/Lunars in Creation is because that's all the people Lunar and the UC found worthy of their Exaltation.<br /> <br /> *I can see Sidereals being limited to a flat 20 per maiden. Silly Maidens liking everything neat and orderly. Of course the Maidens craft their Exalts though events in their lives. I don't see them giving the second breath to some Random Dude they haven't watched and mentored since this dude's first breath. Too risky.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not entirely: There are *around* 400 Lunars. The number of Lunars is vague, but it doesn't necessarily mean it's a changing number (though maybe it could be).<br /> <br /> The other exalts, as far as i know are known set-in-stone numbers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":".  spelling. blaarrrghhh. 03-05-2016, 12:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T10:07:31-08:00","id":842623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/840462-could-an-incarna-make-use-of-an-exigent-exaltation?p=842588#post842588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the end of the day, if you've got an Incarnae suddenly deciding to create a new type of Exalted, it's going to be hard to avoid the implication that this is their &quot;true&quot; Exalted, and hard to avoid the implication of cheapening what it means to be chosen by an Incarnae. I mean -- why are they doing this now? What's the point?</div> </div> </div> </div>Same reason they choose anyone. For Luna it could even be pure whim. But the most interesting possibility that comes to mind is strife among the Fates. Maybe Mars thinks the Sidereals are too beholden to her sisters, who she no longer trusts.<br /> <br /> I expect the Incarnae choose people for positions of power all the time, at least when they're actually doing their jobs. They can hand out titles, divine domains, various blessings, Artifacts, political authority, all sorts of things, They've already got dozens of ways to empower gods and mortals, what's one more?<br /> <br /> Sure, we're using the E-word for this one. But who cares?<br /> <br /> As long as players don't feel like suckers for choosing to play the splat they chose, I don't see much problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T10:47:37-08:00","id":842640,"title":"","content":"The Exigence is there to show that Exaltation is diverse in its manifestation and myriad in its origins. <br /> <br /> Applying the Exigence to everything or trying to measure which Exaltations are more Exalted than others is rather missing the point. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T10:53:27-08:00","id":842645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/840462-could-an-incarna-make-use-of-an-exigent-exaltation?p=842588#post842588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, that doesn't fix it.<br /> <br /> At the end of the day, if you've got an Incarnae suddenly deciding to create a new type of Exalted, it's going to be hard to avoid the implication that this is their &quot;true&quot; Exalted, and hard to avoid the implication of cheapening what it means to be chosen by an Incarnae. I mean -- why are they doing this now? What's the point?<br /> <br /> If your answer is &quot;they just want more power&quot;, <i>ugh</i>. Fine, I'll explain: Part of the purpose of 3e's changes to Exaltation are, I think, to avoid cheapening the Exalted. Exalted are chosen heroes, and Exaltation is a transcendent miracle; it's not a cruise missile. The idea of Luna saying &quot;well, the Lunars are <i>pretty good</i>, but, you know, every little bit helps, so I'm going to squeeze a bit more Exaltation out of the end of the tube and throw some cut-rate New Exalted of Luna out there to help them&quot; inherently cheapens the concept of Exalted and the idea that Luna made an actual meaningful statement by naming the Lunars as her chosen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aquillion, I disagree with a lot of what you say about the nature of Exaltation, but if I could frame this somewhere I would do so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T11:20:30-08:00","id":842655,"title":"","content":"Soooo if I hate animal, werewolf, furcloth barbarian, Artemis and rageroid but love moon symbolism, then is it okay for me to create an Exigent of some other moon-theme god ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T11:28:41-08:00","id":842657,"title":"","content":"You can be a non-beast-barbarian-rage Lunar.<br /> <br /> Unless they really screw up the Lunars book, a civilized scholar/beautiful prince/whatever who was chosen by Luna will be totally playable.<br /> <br /> But yeah, you could totally make an Exigent of some other moon god. You could even use one of the ones Luna ate in Glories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T11:37:17-08:00","id":842663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/840462-could-an-incarna-make-use-of-an-exigent-exaltation?p=842657#post842657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can be a non-beast-barbarian-rage Lunar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even though the devs have said that predicting future splat base on their QC's write-up is a bad idea, I still have a bad feeling about Lunar with all the animal-sounding charm's name.<br /> <br /> Not to mention I don't care about turning into animal that much....<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T11:54:42-08:00","id":842671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/840462-could-an-incarna-make-use-of-an-exigent-exaltation?p=842663#post842663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Even though the devs have said that predicting future splat base on their QC's write-up is a bad idea, I still have a bad feeling about Lunar with all the animal-sounding charm's name.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Lunars will probably still have heavy animal themes. This is not something we should ever expect to go away. They're skinchangers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not to mention I don't care about turning into animal that much.... </div> </div> </div>Then you can just turn into other people! That's a thing. Or not turn into anything at all, although if you don't want to shapeshift into anything, well... the Lunar Exalted may not be right for you. They can't encompass all moon symbolism into one Exalt type.<br /> <br /> You could totally make an Exigent of some other moon-associated god, tho. I bet you could make a God of Tides or something.<br /> <br /> ... actually, hmm.<br /> <br /> This is verging on special snowflake-ism, but if someone came to me and said &quot;I'd like to create an Exigent of Zatesh of the Doorways&quot; I would <i>consider</i> hearing them out. Because the concept of a devoured aspect of a God-That-Never-Was somehow stealing the divine fire and empowering an Exigent even though it doesn't actually exist and is merely a subsumed aspect of the God that absorbed it to become the moon sounds like some <i>choice</i> shit to me.<br /> <br /> But that's a bit different than Luna just deciding she wants some more Exalts and getting her buddy the UCS to fork over some Exigences.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T12:01:24-08:00","id":842672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/840462-could-an-incarna-make-use-of-an-exigent-exaltation?p=842663#post842663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Even though the devs have said that predicting future splat base on their QC's write-up is a bad idea, I still have a bad feeling about Lunar with all the animal-sounding charm's name.<br /> <br /> Not to mention I don't care about turning into animal that much....<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It sounds like Lunars are not for you. <br /> <br /> What are the moon themes you do like?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T12:22:00-08:00","id":842677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/840462-could-an-incarna-make-use-of-an-exigent-exaltation?p=842671#post842671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is verging on special snowflake-ism, but if someone came to me and said &quot;I'd like to create an Exigent of Zatesh of the Doorways&quot; I would <i>consider</i> hearing them out. Because the concept of a devoured aspect of a God-That-Never-Was somehow stealing the divine fire and empowering an Exigent even though it doesn't actually exist and is merely a subsumed aspect of the God that absorbed it to become the moon sounds like some <i>choice</i> shit to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there is a goddess of twilight in canon so I figure that there are probably other deities for the various phase of the sun/moon. I don't really attach to the whole &quot;Chosen of the Moon&quot; thing, I just want moon aesthetic in my character tbh...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/840462-could-an-incarna-make-use-of-an-exigent-exaltation?p=842672#post842672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It sounds like Lunars are not for you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have never wanted to play a Lunar to be exact, it's more like I want to play a character who has moon symbolism and the Lunar already has a trademark on that. I guess I can just play a Sid or Solar who have a giant silver disk in their anima, but people seems to frown on that kind of &quot;your anima has the wrong color&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/840462-could-an-incarna-make-use-of-an-exigent-exaltation?p=842672#post842672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are the moon themes you do like?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly love, elegant, dream and illusion, I think the final two got discarded by the devs as things that Ex3 Lunar won't be focus on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T19:08:36-08:00","id":842828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/840462-could-an-incarna-make-use-of-an-exigent-exaltation?p=842677#post842677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have never wanted to play a Lunar to be exact, it's more like I want to play a character who has moon symbolism and the Lunar already has a trademark on that. I guess I can just play a Sid or Solar who have a giant silver disk in their anima, but people seems to frown on that kind of &quot;your anima has the wrong color&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Brilliant white&quot; is one of the options listed for an Eclipse caste, if that helps.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/840462-could-an-incarna-make-use-of-an-exigent-exaltation?p=842677#post842677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mostly love, elegant, dream and illusion, I think the final two got discarded by the devs as things that Ex3 Lunar won't be focus on.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I had to pick a canon god that fits these themes it would probably be Yaogin the Fair, Bearer of the Lapis Ewer. He's the god of beautiful dreams, and quite elegant and beautiful himself.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":2093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","user":"Crumplepunch","date":". 03-05-2016, 10:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T20:32:46-08:00","id":842845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/840462-could-an-incarna-make-use-of-an-exigent-exaltation?p=841560#post841560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm confused do you not want this thread to continue? I am getting a sense you want me to drop all discussion for some reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not my intent at all. I was merely passing on facts. If your intent is to make an Incarnae Exigent that is only valid at your table, you're more then welcome to do so.<br /> <br /> I view Exigents a bit differently then you appear to though. You said to CountAlucard that an Incarnae's Exigent would be different from their current Exalted. There is nothing to prove that case though. I don't believe gods pick and choose what abilities to give their Exigents. Rather they imbue the exaltation with their power, and their purviews imprint upon the exaltation. By that standard, &quot;if&quot; an Incarnae did make an Exigent, they would be identical to their current Chosen in almost every way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-06T03:06:34-08:00","id":842933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TalosX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/840462-could-an-incarna-make-use-of-an-exigent-exaltation?p=842845#post842845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I view Exigents a bit differently then you appear to though. You said to CountAlucard that an Incarnae's Exigent would be different from their current Exalted. There is nothing to prove that case though. I don't believe gods pick and choose what abilities to give their Exigents. Rather they imbue the exaltation with their power, and their purviews imprint upon the exaltation. By that standard, &quot;if&quot; an Incarnae did make an Exigent, they would be identical to their current Chosen in almost every way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Conversely, is it actually that good if the Incarna made no meaningful choices in the nature of what their Chosen were actually like?<br /> <br /> While people can go a bit extreme with the idea of &quot;The Incarna designed their Chosen to do *exactly* this particular role&quot;, I wouldn't want to lose the idea that they each intentionally decided to have specifically a certain kind of Chosen. <br /> <br /> Rather than, y'know, they chose to Exalt people and then what fell out of that, what kind of Exalted and the nature of those Exalted, was pretty much something they had no role in deciding or intending. <br /> <br /> I assume people who play the game want to be the Chosen of Luna, etc. because Luna wanted those type of Chosen, not just, well, given here nature that's all she was ever going to get. <br /> You don't have to go to either extreme of them making no choices in what their Chosen would be like, every absolute little thing and ever potential within each of the Chosen being a choice. (And if they did make some choices, possibly we can imagine they could've made other ones.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-06T07:15:56-08:00","id":842969,"title":"","content":"So, since the question of a canonical answer to the Exigents of the Incarna has been repeated ad nauseam... I'll offer my opinion on it instead. Yes. The Exigence of Mars is a Chosen of Mars. The Exigence of Luna is a Chosen of Luna. There is no identifiable difference unless there is a way for a character to detect and distinguish between Exaltation and Exigence.<br /> <br /> As for your other Premise, I love the idea of an Exigence of a concert of Gods. More interesting* to me would be the Exigent of the Incarna if you were to combine the two premises together.<br /> *Interesting in that I would enjoy the novelty and narrative of such a character, much in the same way I enjoy the Scarlet Empress.<br /> <br /> But then again, I'm wait for the Exigent Book so that I can create my Exigent of Lytek.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/15.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2104-tenkage","name":"Tenkage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2104_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-06T07:41:46-08:00","id":842980,"title":"","content":"Exigence is what you give a god who cannot create Exalted on there own, and might have at least some reference to the idea of it being an emergency, one-off thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T07:38:20-08:00","id":843425,"title":"","content":"Hence the name &quot;Exigent.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T08:14:03-08:00","id":843444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tenkage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/840462-could-an-incarna-make-use-of-an-exigent-exaltation?p=842969#post842969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, since the question of a canonical answer to the Exigents of the Incarna has been repeated ad nauseam... I'll offer my opinion on it instead. Yes. The Exigence of Mars is a Chosen of Mars. The Exigence of Luna is a Chosen of Luna. There is no identifiable difference unless there is a way for a character to detect and distinguish between Exaltation and Exigence.<br /> <br /> As for your other Premise, I love the idea of an Exigence of a concert of Gods. More interesting* to me would be the Exigent of the Incarna if you were to combine the two premises together.<br /> *Interesting in that I would enjoy the novelty and narrative of such a character, much in the same way I enjoy the Scarlet Empress.<br /> <br /> But then again, I'm wait for the Exigent Book so that I can create my Exigent of Lytek.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hey now. Don't go having alternate ideas that might lead to fun. The Canon Police and the Devthink Priesthood are already after you, see?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T16:51:17-08:00","id":843681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/840462-could-an-incarna-make-use-of-an-exigent-exaltation?p=843444#post843444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Hey now. Don't go having alternate ideas that might lead to fun. The Canon Police and the Devthink Priesthood are already after you, see?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm always puzzled when people respond in this manner...<br /> <br /> Is it unusual for me to assume that people who ask questions like &quot;can something do someshit&quot; are interested in canon, dev guidelines or community consensus?<br /> <br /> If all your interest in the matter is how fun it would be in your table, the answer is always yes for fun, so why bother asking?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T16:59:30-08:00","id":843686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/840462-could-an-incarna-make-use-of-an-exigent-exaltation?p=843681#post843681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'm always puzzled when people respond in this manner...<br /> <br /> Is it unusual for me to assume that people who ask questions like &quot;can something do someshit&quot; are interested in canon, dev guidelines or community consensus?<br /> <br /> If all your interest in the matter is how fun it would be in your table, the answer is always yes for fun, so why bother asking?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Usually when I ask similar questions, it's more along the lines of &quot;If I change this, what breaks in the system?&quot; Hopefully people will find all the flaws in my idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T17:30:07-08:00","id":843703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/840462-could-an-incarna-make-use-of-an-exigent-exaltation?p=843681#post843681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm always puzzled when people respond in this manner...<br /> <br /> Is it unusual for me to assume that people who ask questions like &quot;can something do someshit&quot; are interested in canon, dev guidelines or community consensus?<br /> <br /> If all your interest in the matter is how fun it would be in your table, the answer is always yes for fun, so why bother asking?</div> </div> </div> </div>I tend to respond to such questions with two responses. The first, if their is a canon ruling on the question, I reiterate it. Not to discourage creative gaming, but because maybe the OP simply didn't know their was a canon ruling that answered their question. My second response is usually on my personal views and thoughts on the subject (ie. if I've house-ruled something or if I have a viewpoint on the subject matter, etc).<br /> <br /> I like a lot of the canon material, but no one but my group and I know what works best for our table. In short, canon material is useful and provides a solid guideline. However, games are meant to be fun, so do whatever you need to do to have a great time at your table! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T17:49:42-08:00","id":843709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/840462-could-an-incarna-make-use-of-an-exigent-exaltation?p=842933#post842933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Conversely, is it actually that good if the Incarna made no meaningful choices in the nature of what their Chosen were actually like?<br /> <br /> While people can go a bit extreme with the idea of &quot;The Incarna designed their Chosen to do *exactly* this particular role&quot;, I wouldn't want to lose the idea that they each intentionally decided to have specifically a certain kind of Chosen.<br /> <br /> Rather than, y'know, they chose to Exalt people and then what fell out of that, what kind of Exalted and the nature of those Exalted, was pretty much something they had no role in deciding or intending.<br /> <br /> I assume people who play the game want to be the Chosen of Luna, etc. because Luna wanted those type of Chosen, not just, well, given here nature that's all she was ever going to get.<br /> You don't have to go to either extreme of them making no choices in what their Chosen would be like, every absolute little thing and ever potential within each of the Chosen being a choice. (And if they did make some choices, possibly we can imagine they could've made other ones.)</div> </div> </div> </div>It's an interesting thought. The UCS and Luna both kind of already did break up their purviews by the Castes. Though the Maidens have pretty focused purviews by design. From a lore standpoint, wouldn't any Exigent created by the Incarnae be weaker then the current Chosen!? The original Exalts were created to fight the war against the Primordials. The Incarnae wouldn't have held back in creating their ultimate weapons when you consider enemy they were facing. The original Exalts are very likely the upper limit of each Incarnae's power to create.<br /> <br /> With all that in mind, why would any of the Incarnae create an Exigent that is very likely weaker with a smaller purview focus, then their current Chosen? This is one canon ruling that will likely stick at my table, because it simply doesn't make sense for the Incarnae to need an Exigent when they already have their own Exalts to call on... not to mention that being an Incarnae means they could order any number of gods and spirits about as well!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T04:12:06-08:00","id":843889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/840462-could-an-incarna-make-use-of-an-exigent-exaltation?p=843681#post843681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm always puzzled when people respond in this manner...</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm mostly amused when I see it these days because 2e was the glory days of the canon police.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T08:04:47-08:00","id":843967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/840462-could-an-incarna-make-use-of-an-exigent-exaltation?p=843444#post843444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Hey now. Don't go having alternate ideas that might lead to fun. The Canon Police and the Devthink Priesthood are already after you, see?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Dragon Blooded have no souls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T14:41:39-08:00","id":844157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/840462-could-an-incarna-make-use-of-an-exigent-exaltation?p=843967#post843967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Dragon Blooded have no souls.</div> </div> </div> </div>FIREDUST CAN'T MELT JADE BEAMS!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T04:33:03-08:00","id":844431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/840462-could-an-incarna-make-use-of-an-exigent-exaltation?p=843967#post843967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dragon Blooded have no souls.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why the Dragons used Exigence to make themselves actual Exalted - and Celestial level, no less!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T06:33:59-08:00","id":844474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/840462-could-an-incarna-make-use-of-an-exigent-exaltation?p=844431#post844431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is why the Dragons used Exigence to make themselves actual Exalted - and Celestial level, no less!</div> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"ma