3-12T03:02:22-08:00","id":846011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/840462-could-an-incarna-make-use-of-an-exigent-exaltation?p=846006#post846006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Conky can't be such a cool guy !</div> </div> </div> </div>Conky's a total bro!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T03:26:20-08:00","id":846016,"title":"","content":"I would tend to portray the Exigence as almost solely the province of the Sun, as I would see his whole King of Heaven thing coming from him being the more public and sociable of them, with the others having a more introverted and mysterious character. I would think of the Flame as something that has to be asked for, and Luna and the Maidens not exactly being figure whom you can petition. That's just my sense of how to maintain a consistency in their distinct characteristics and position in the Celestial Order. This is a schema in which it still might be fitting for one of the other Incarnae to endorse a small god's petition before the Unconquered Sun, which may or may not have been solicited, but the buck still stops with him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T03:45:49-08:00","id":846017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/840462-could-an-incarna-make-use-of-an-exigent-exaltation?p=846016#post846016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would tend to portray the Exigence as almost solely the province of the Sun, as I would see his whole King of Heaven thing coming from him being the more public and sociable of them, with the others having a more introverted and mysterious character. I would think of the Flame as something that has to be asked for, and Luna and the Maidens not exactly being figure whom you can petition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Saaay, does the characterization of Luna as &quot;The Fun Guy&quot; in the fanbase supported by any books ?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T05:27:32-08:00","id":846031,"title":"","content":"Not really. Luna is ever-changing, unpredictable, and mercurial. There are various <i>aspects</i> of Luna, one of which is probably about Bacchus-style revelry, but overall they tend more towards transgressive, transcendent, savage or bloodthirsty.<br /> <br /> Something like just generic &quot;party animal&quot; is fun for forum jokes, but doesn't fit the Incarnae very well for canon -- they're not <i>that</i> approachable or easily-relatable; they're meant to be distant and somewhat intimidating figures. Luna should generally evoke that quote from CS Lewis about Aslan about him not being a tame lion -- there's definitely a party side to her, but like with Bacchus, there's a degree of danger there. Luna's revelry would probably involve stepping outside of social norms and letting everything out -- it'd be something that people might do for her festival, but not something casual like you'd get from a fun guy at a bar. It'd be a revelry so deep and primal that it would be like a religious experience. (Which is appropriate what with her being, you know, a god.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 03-12-2016, 08:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T06:45:53-08:00","id":846055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/840462-could-an-incarna-make-use-of-an-exigent-exaltation?p=845904#post845904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would actually be totally comfortable with &quot;sometimes Sol gives the Flame of Exigence to the other Incarnae to bestow as they see fit, even to honor requests from deities that he personally would not have approved, because they are his comrades and friends, and though he is the chief of the gods, he values the fact that their perspectives are not his perspectives.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I would prefer to avoid going back to effectively &quot;Nice Guy Buddy Jesus UCS.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T08:13:01-08:00","id":846071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">does the characterization of Luna as &quot;The Fun Guy&quot; in the fanbase supported by any books</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm not sure what that means exactly, but... yes? Glories portrays her as having a certain playful side in general, a tendency to go amongst the gods and stir things up, and as the one among the Incarnae who kind of prods within their little group. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">overall they tend more towards transgressive, transcendent, savage or bloodthirsty.</div> </div> </div> </div> The core Luna is described as savage and seductive. Her most consistent traits are said to be her positive relationships with her peers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T12:33:55-08:00","id":846223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/840462-could-an-incarna-make-use-of-an-exigent-exaltation?p=846016#post846016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Luna and the Maidens not exactly being figure whom you can petition.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the Maidens are still running the Bureau, not being able to petition them for stuff is going to be problematic from an organizational standpoint.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah I would prefer to avoid going back to effectively &quot;Nice Guy Buddy Jesus UCS.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, because the UCS respecting and valuing his fellow Incarnae and sometimes giving them nice stuff to spread around is <i>precisely</i> that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T12:40:45-08:00","id":846226,"title":"","content":"I figure I would have to invent a God of Light in order to have a Lux Exalted. The Unconquered Sun's purview includes illumination, but it's quite specifically golden sunlight rather than universal illumination. I have a vision of an Exalt who is light, airy, ethereal, et cetera with themes of the colour white, crystal/glass, air, immateriality, et cetera.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u263e</span></span></b></span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/438-wulf","name":"wulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T13:08:11-08:00","id":846240,"title":"","content":"IRC there's some writer commentary (John Morke) on the Sidereals having a political hand on the Exigence, as a political process, so from that I'd imagine it's not improbable that their patron goddesses and the Lunars' patron goddess, also have some hand in it. We'll have to see what it actually is in their book though (whether the Sidereals and other gods are involved in the process of managing Exigence, or just involved in managing Exigents).<br /> <br /> Re: a god of light, I tend to think the gods will be things that are specifically relevant to people's lives. Like you have a god of storms (because they can destroy your harvest, sink your boat and have a resonance of might in the mind of man), while you don't have a god of rainbows because, who cares? (unless you're in some variant area of Creation where they have deeply significant magical power), although the god of rain certainly has a rainbow for his bow and a god of prosperity can wield it as her symbol and so on. So I find it easier to see gods of windows, vision, glass, torches and candles and other such things that have an immediate and concrete use to people, than an overarching god of light, and I can imagine there'd be cool things you could to with that... Or they could even be unified under a single god, but he's the god of those separate things combined in one purview, rather than the god of light as such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T13:13:11-08:00","id":846242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/840462-could-an-incarna-make-use-of-an-exigent-exaltation?p=846226#post846226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I figure I would have to invent a God of Light in order to have a Lux Exalted. The Unconquered Sun's purview includes illumination, but it's quite specifically golden sunlight rather than universal illumination. I have a vision of an Exalt who is light, airy, ethereal, et cetera with themes of the colour white, crystal/glass, air, immateriality, et cetera.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dude.<br /> <br /> <i>Lighthouse God</i>.<br /> <br /> A friend of mine noted that you can actually get some good themes out of a lighthouse. You've got illumination, safely guiding people, protection, sanctuary...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T13:16:46-08:00","id":846244,"title":"","content":"That's a great idea!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u263e</span></span></b></span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/438-wulf","name":"wulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T18:42:00-08:00","id":846370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/840462-could-an-incarna-make-use-of-an-exigent-exaltation?p=846242#post846242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dude.<br /> <br /> <i>Lighthouse God</i>.<br /> <br /> A friend of mine noted that you can actually get some good themes out of a lighthouse. You've got illumination, safely guiding people, protection, sanctuary...</div> </div> </div> </div>Kyman, you are the <i>best one.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T19:16:19-08:00","id":846381,"title":"","content":"...<br /> 2e just made me facepalm again.<br /> <br /> The Exigent idea reminded me of the First Age lighthouses that were built all over the place keep Erembour away, so I went to look that up only to discover that Erembour doesn't actually have an escape clause. Thus these lighthouses only existed to protect the city against an extremely specific form of malicious action from a Solar Circle Sorcerer (because sending Ligier would be considered rude?) or to safeguard against an escape clause that didn't exist.<br /> <br /> Sorry. I thought I had the basis of a cool idea of the Exigent in question being from the god of one of those lighthouses calling upon the Exigence when Erembour returns to Creation but the details push their existence towards a magitech version of <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fm2W0sq9ddU\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> scenario than an actual form of defence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 03-13-2016, 10:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T19:35:00-08:00","id":846395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the Maidens are still running the Bureau, not being able to petition them for stuff is going to be problematic from an organizational standpoint.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm torn between a response of &quot;that's what people like Nara-O are for&quot; and &quot;Age of Sorrows&quot;. Either way; the Maidens are the ultimate heads of the Bureau of Destiny, but that still seems to consist largely of enigmatic instructions that are beyond question, and leading by example that subordinates have to intuitively extrapolate policy trends from. For the most part, the command of the Maidens does not seem to consist of reading reports and signing off on paperwork; they are the weavers of the raw substance of existence, and lend it its nuances.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T20:20:42-08:00","id":846410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/840462-could-an-incarna-make-use-of-an-exigent-exaltation?p=846370#post846370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Kyman, you are the <i>best one.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Thank <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar280_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"280\" data-vbnamecard=\"280\">Valles</a>, actually. It was HIS idea, I'm just parroting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T09:26:26-07:00","id":846601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/840462-could-an-incarna-make-use-of-an-exigent-exaltation?p=843681#post843681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'm always puzzled when people respond in this manner...<br /> <br /> Is it unusual for me to assume that people who ask questions like &quot;can something do someshit&quot; are interested in canon, dev guidelines or community consensus?<br /> <br /> If all your interest in the matter is how fun it would be in your table, the answer is always yes for fun, so why bother asking?</div> </div> </div> </div>So, on the most direct, level, yes, as long as you're having fun, your table can do whatever. On the surface, that might seem to negate the need for conversation.<br /> <br /> But of course we want to converse about the game we love and play (at least in theory we love it and play it). Speaking just for myself, I'm quite willing to step all over canon for the sake of my story, but I would like to step on canon intentionally, not accidentally. One reason I post ideas on this forum is for people to point out how my changes might screw up other parts of the setting in ways I had not contemplated. I also post ideas to get feedback, see if anyone else has done similar things, etc.<br /> <br /> It's always valid to have a conversation about what the default game supports. My comment was aimed rather at the judgmental culture that's sprung up on this forum, where deviations from dev intent are seen as inferior or wrong. Since the backer PDF has dropped, there has been a drastic uptick in instances of people telling other people they are playing the game wrong. Not &quot;this isn't what canon supports.&quot; But, saying or implying if they don't like a system or setting conceit that they are playing the game wrong and should play it another way. My comment was directed at that undercurrent of seeming condescension.<br /> <br /> Sure, let's have all the conversation, including what's canon. But let's do it from the standpoint that we are here to have fun with our game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T11:28:40-07:00","id":846647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/840462-could-an-incarna-make-use-of-an-exigent-exaltation?p=846601#post846601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, on the most direct, level, yes, as long as you're having fun, your table can do whatever. On the surface, that might seem to negate the need for conversation.<br /> <br /> But of course we want to converse about the game we love and play (at least in theory we love it and play it). Speaking just for myself, I'm quite willing to step all over canon for the sake of my story, but I would like to step on canon intentionally, not accidentally. One reason I post ideas on this forum is for people to point out how my changes might screw up other parts of the setting in ways I had not contemplated. I also post ideas to get feedback, see if anyone else has done similar things, etc.<br /> <br /> It's always valid to have a conversation about what the default game supports. My comment was aimed rather at the judgmental culture that's sprung up on this forum, where deviations from dev intent are seen as inferior or wrong. Since the backer PDF has dropped, there has been a drastic uptick in instances of people telling other people they are playing the game wrong. Not &quot;this isn't what canon supports.&quot; But, saying or implying if they don't like a system or setting conceit that they are playing the game wrong and should play it another way. My comment was directed at that undercurrent of seeming condescension.<br /> <br /> Sure, let's have all the conversation, including what's canon. But let's do it from the standpoint that we are here to have fun with our game.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the thing, It's been a long while since I saw people outright stating someone &quot;can't do this&quot; because canon says otherwise, though I might have overlooked some incident.<br /> <br /> We have one common ground, a foundation, on which we have setting discussion, and that's canon.<br /> <br /> When someone questions if something would act/behave in some sort of way or be able/willing to do something, I always assume the person is interested in the canon response. Most people that respond will be the ones who were interested enough to have read about the matter and cared enough to learn and remember it.<br /> <br /> The answer being negative, as in &quot;no, X doesn't work like that because of this and that&quot; is not curbstomping fun and keeping it down. It is just the canon facts, if you want it to be different at your table go ahead. Other helpful answers might even add &quot; and I would be reluctant/would not allow it because of that and this&quot;.<br /> <br /> Now if you say &quot;I know the Incarnae don't use the Exigence in canon, but what would change in the setting if I were to change that?&quot;, that's a whole different question. You might still get people opining that you shouldn't do it for any sort of reasons but, the premise of the question being well defined, it will generate more appropriate answers.<br /> <br /> What I'm trying to get at is that negative (as in opposite to affirmative, not moody, etc...) answers aren't always fun police at work. Some(most of the?) times they're just the right answers within the assumed context.<br /> <br /> PS It is very difficult to express the right tone through the written medium of forum boards. Many times I gave up responding to something because it just read too confrontational, even though I was trying to be anything but. I think the more accustomed to this people get the thicker their forum post reading skin should become. And then you can always choose to not engage with someone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T06:45:12-07:00","id":847045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/840462-could-an-incarna-make-use-of-an-exigent-exaltation?p=846381#post846381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...<br /> 2e just made me facepalm again.<br /> <br /> The Exigent idea reminded me of the First Age lighthouses that were built all over the place keep Erembour away, so I went to look that up only to discover that Erembour doesn't actually have an escape clause. Thus these lighthouses only existed to protect the city against an extremely specific form of malicious action from a Solar Circle Sorcerer (because sending Ligier would be considered rude?) or to safeguard against an escape clause that didn't exist.<br /> <br /> Sorry. I thought I had the basis of a cool idea of the Exigent in question being from the god of one of those lighthouses calling upon the Exigence when Erembour returns to Creation but the details push their existence towards a magitech version of <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fm2W0sq9ddU\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> scenario than an actual form of defence.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought those lighthouse's job is to dispel Erembour's jazz which has a tendency to drift from Hell to Creation ?<br /> <br /> Hmmm, I wonder if the book plan to go back to 1ed Erembour who have an escape clause but rarely used it and not so terribly...mustache twirling. Reading her entry in RoGD makes me imagine people hearing the drifting music will turn into monster who can't abide the sun, but in GoD it just mostly lure sheeps to omen dogs and call people to dark profession.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T09:09:39-07:00","id":847115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/840462-could-an-incarna-make-use-of-an-exigent-exaltation?p=846601#post846601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since the backer PDF has dropped, there has been a drastic uptick in instances of people telling other people they are playing the game wrong. Not &quot;this isn't what canon supports.&quot; But, saying or implying if they don't like a system or setting conceit that they are playing the game wrong and should play it another way. My comment was directed at that undercurrent of seeming condescension.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly I haven't seen this at all since the backer PDF came out. Which isn't it say it hasn't happened a couple times but id sure remember if it was happening often. <br /> <br /> Maybe it's in all those craft complaint/fix threads that I've generally been ignoring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T12:47:26-07:00","id":847243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/840462-could-an-incarna-make-use-of-an-exigent-exaltation?p=847045#post847045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought those lighthouse's job is to dispel Erembour's jazz which has a tendency to drift from Hell to Creation ?<br /> <br /> Hmmm, I wonder if the book plan to go back to 1ed Erembour who have an escape clause but rarely used it and not so terribly...mustache twirling. Reading her entry in RoGD makes me imagine people hearing the drifting music will turn into monster who can't abide the sun, but in GoD it just mostly lure sheeps to omen dogs and call people to dark profession.</div> </div> </div> </div>The whole point of it being an actual lighthouse is the light itself playing upon her biggest weakness and stopping her. You'd only need the klaxons if the only problem was the music of her horn.<br /> <br /> It's a shame really, the notion of an ancient lighthouse that's way too far inland to make any sense in a more conventional role could be a fun story hook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 03-14-2016, 03:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T13:05:50-07:00","id":847255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/840462-could-an-incarna-make-use-of-an-exigent-exaltation?p=847115#post847115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly I haven't seen this at all since the backer PDF came out. Which isn't it say it hasn't happened a couple times but id sure remember if it was happening often.<br /> <br /> Maybe it's in all those craft complaint/fix threads that I've generally been ignoring.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a hefty chunk of it. You saved yourself some sanity/Willpower points avoiding them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"